{"status":"ok","message-type":"work-list","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"facets":{},"total-results":2323867,"items":[{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,11,15]],"date-time":"2026-11-15T11:16:20Z","timestamp":1794741380293,"version":"4.9.1"},"reference-count":20,"publisher":"MIT Press","issue":"8","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Neural Computation"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[1997,11,1]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>Learning to store information over extended time intervals by recurrent backpropagation takes a very long time, mostly because of insufficient, decaying error backflow. We briefly review Hochreiter's (1991) analysis of this problem, then address it by introducing a novel, efficient, gradient based method called long short-term memory (LSTM). Truncating the gradient where this does not do harm, LSTM can learn to bridge minimal time lags in excess of 1000 discrete-time steps by enforcing constant error flow through constant error carousels within special units. Multiplicative gate units learn to open and close access to the constant error flow. LSTM is local in space and time; its computational complexity per time step and weight is O. 1. Our experiments with artificial data involve local, distributed, real-valued, and noisy pattern representations. In comparisons with real-time recurrent learning, back propagation through time, recurrent cascade correlation, Elman nets, and neural sequence chunking, LSTM leads to many more successful runs, and learns much faster. LSTM also solves complex, artificial long-time-lag tasks that have never been solved by previous recurrent network algorithms.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1162\/neco.1997.9.8.1735","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2006,5,29]],"date-time":"2006-05-29T11:29:41Z","timestamp":1148902181000},"page":"1735-1780","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":90845,"title":["Long Short-Term Memory"],"prefix":"10.1162","volume":"9","author":[{"given":"Sepp","family":"Hochreiter","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Fakult\u00e4t f\u00fcr Informatik, Technische Universit\u00e4t M\u00fcnchen, 80290 M\u00fcnchen, Germany"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"J\u00fcrgen","family":"Schmidhuber","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"IDSIA, Corso Elvezia 36, 6900 Lugano, Switzerland"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"281","reference":[{"key":"p_2","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"526","DOI":"10.1162\/neco.1991.3.4.526","volume":"3","author":"Baldi P.","year":"1991","journal-title":"Neural Computation"},{"issue":"2","key":"p_4","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"157","DOI":"10.1109\/72.279181","volume":"5","author":"Bengio Y.","year":"1994","journal-title":"IEEE Transactions on Neural Networks"},{"key":"p_5","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"372","DOI":"10.1162\/neco.1989.1.3.372","volume":"1","author":"Cleeremans A.","year":"1989","journal-title":"Neural Computation"},{"key":"p_8","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"375","DOI":"10.1016\/0893-6080(89)90022-1","volume":"2","author":"Doya K.","year":"1989","journal-title":"Neural Networks"},{"key":"p_15","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"23","DOI":"10.1016\/0893-6080(90)90044-L","volume":"3","author":"Lang K.","year":"1990","journal-title":"Neural Networks"},{"key":"p_16","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"1329","DOI":"10.1109\/72.548162","volume":"7","author":"Lin T.","year":"1996","journal-title":"IEEE Transactions on Neural Networks"},{"issue":"4","key":"p_17","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"849","DOI":"10.1142\/S0218001493000431","volume":"7","author":"Miller C. B.","year":"1993","journal-title":"International Journal of Pattern Recognition and Artificial Intelligence"},{"key":"p_18","first-page":"349","volume":"3","author":"Mozer M. C.","year":"1989","journal-title":"Complex Systems"},{"issue":"2","key":"p_20","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"263","DOI":"10.1162\/neco.1989.1.2.263","volume":"1","author":"Pearlmutter B. A.","year":"1989","journal-title":"Neural Computation"},{"issue":"5","key":"p_21","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"1212","DOI":"10.1109\/72.410363","volume":"6","author":"Pearlmutter B. A.","year":"1995","journal-title":"IEEE Transactions on Neural Networks"},{"issue":"59","key":"p_22","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"2229","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevLett.59.2229","volume":"19","author":"Pineda F. J.","year":"1987","journal-title":"Physical Review Letters"},{"key":"p_23","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"216","DOI":"10.1016\/0885-064X(88)90021-0","volume":"4","author":"Pineda F. J.","year":"1988","journal-title":"Journal of Complexity"},{"issue":"2","key":"p_26","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"279","DOI":"10.1109\/72.279191","volume":"5","author":"Puskorius G. V.","year":"1994","journal-title":"IEEE Transactions on Neural Networks"},{"issue":"4","key":"p_29","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"403","DOI":"10.1080\/09540098908915650","volume":"1","author":"Schmidhuber J.","year":"1989","journal-title":"Connection Science"},{"issue":"2","key":"p_30","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"243","DOI":"10.1162\/neco.1992.4.2.243","volume":"4","author":"Schmidhuber J.","year":"1992","journal-title":"Neural Computation"},{"issue":"2","key":"p_31","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"234","DOI":"10.1162\/neco.1992.4.2.234","volume":"4","author":"Schmidhuber J.","year":"1992","journal-title":"Neural Computation"},{"issue":"2","key":"p_36","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"125","DOI":"10.1142\/S0129065789000037","volume":"1","author":"Smith A. W.","year":"1989","journal-title":"International Journal of Neural Systems"},{"key":"p_38","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"406","DOI":"10.1162\/neco.1992.4.3.406","volume":"4","author":"Watrous R. L.","year":"1992","journal-title":"Neural Computation"},{"key":"p_39","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"339","DOI":"10.1016\/0893-6080(88)90007-X","volume":"1","author":"Werbos P. J.","year":"1988","journal-title":"Neural Networks"},{"key":"p_41","first-page":"491","volume":"4","author":"Williams R. J.","year":"1990","journal-title":"Neural Computation"}],"container-title":["Neural Computation"],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/www.mitpressjournals.org\/doi\/pdf\/10.1162\/neco.1997.9.8.1735","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2021,3,12]],"date-time":"2021-03-12T16:34:33Z","timestamp":1615566873000},"score":39.051647,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/direct.mit.edu\/neco\/article\/9\/8\/1735-1780\/6109"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[1997,11,1]]},"references-count":20,"journal-issue":{"issue":"8","published-print":{"date-parts":[[1997,11,1]]}},"alternative-id":["10.1162\/neco.1997.9.8.1735"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1162\/neco.1997.9.8.1735","relation":{"is-referenced-by":[{"id-type":"doi","id":"10.1038\/s41598-026-35386-9","asserted-by":"object"}]},"ISSN":["0899-7667","1530-888X"],"issn-type":[{"value":"0899-7667","type":"print"},{"value":"1530-888X","type":"electronic"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[1997,11,1]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,1]],"date-time":"2026-10-01T00:46:50Z","timestamp":1790815610828,"version":"4.1.0"},"reference-count":53,"publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media LLC","issue":"7-8","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2021,5,17]],"date-time":"2021-05-17T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1621209600000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2021,5,17]],"date-time":"2021-05-17T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1621209600000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0"}],"funder":[{"name":"Johannes Kepler University Linz"}],"content-domain":{"domain":["link.springer.com"],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["\u00d6sterr Wasser- und Abfallw"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2021,8]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Zusammenfassung<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>Methoden der k\u00fcnstlichen Intelligenz haben sich in den letzten Jahren zu essenziellen Bestandteilen fast aller Bereiche von Wissenschaft und Technik entwickelt. Dies gilt auch f\u00fcr die Hydrologie: Vielschichtige neuronale Netzwerke \u2013\u00a0auch bekannt als Modelle des Deep Learning\u00a0\u2013 erm\u00f6glichen hier Vorhersagen von Niederschlagsabflussmengen in zuvor unerreichter Pr\u00e4zision.<\/jats:p>\n                  <jats:p>Dieser Beitrag beleuchtet das Potenzial von Deep Learning f\u00fcr wasserwirtschaftliche Anwendungen. Der erste Teil des Artikels zeigt, wie sogenannte Long Short-Term Memory-Netzwerke \u2013\u00a0eine spezifisch f\u00fcr Zeitreihen entwickelte Methode des Deep Learnings\u00a0\u2013 f\u00fcr die Niederschlags-Abfluss-Modellierung verwendet werden, und wie diese f\u00fcr eine Reihe hydrologischer Probleme bessere Ergebnisse als jedes andere bekannte hydrologische Modell erzielen. Der zweite Teil demonstriert wesentliche Eigenschaften der Long Short-Term Memory-Netzwerke. Zum einen zeigen wir, dass diese Netzwerke beliebige Daten verarbeiten k\u00f6nnen. Dies erlaubt es, m\u00f6gliche synergetische Effekte aus unterschiedlichen meteorologischen Datens\u00e4tzen zu extrahieren und damit die Modellg\u00fcte zu verbessern. Zum anderen stellen wir dar, wie relevante hydrologische Prozesse (wie z.\u202fB. das Akkumulieren und Schmelzen von Schnee) innerhalb der Modelle abgebildet werden, ohne dass diese spezifisch darauf trainiert wurden.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1007\/s00506-021-00767-z","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2021,5,17]],"date-time":"2021-05-17T05:02:17Z","timestamp":1621227737000},"page":"270-280","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1007\/springer_crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":13,"title":["Niederschlags-Abfluss-Modellierung mit Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM)","Rainfall-Runoff modeling with Long Short-Term Memory Networks (LSTM)\u2014an overview"],"prefix":"10.1007","volume":"73","author":[{"given":"Frederik","family":"Kratzert","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Martin","family":"Gauch","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Grey","family":"Nearing","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Sepp","family":"Hochreiter","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Daniel","family":"Klotz","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"297","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2021,5,17]]},"reference":[{"issue":"10","key":"767_CR1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"5293","DOI":"10.5194\/hess-21-5293-2017","volume":"21","author":"N Addor","year":"2017","unstructured":"Addor, N., Newman, A. J., Mizukami, N. & Clark, M. P. (2017): The CAMELS data set: catchment attributes and meteorology for large-sample studies, Hydrology and Earth System Sciences 21(10), 5293\u20135313.","journal-title":"Hydrology and Earth System Sciences"},{"issue":"5","key":"767_CR2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"1338","DOI":"10.1002\/15-1061","volume":"26","author":"R Behnke","year":"2016","unstructured":"Behnke, R., Vavrus, S., Allstadt, A., Albright, T., Thogmartin, W. E. & Radeloff, V. C. (2016): Evaluation of downscaled, gridded climate data for the conterminous United States, Ecological applications 26(5), 1338\u20131351.","journal-title":"Ecological applications"},{"key":"767_CR59","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Beven, K. (2016): Facets of uncertainty: epistemic uncertainty, non-stationarity, likelihood, hy